  "description": "Flat Amazon floodplain forest (várzea): tall kapok and sandbox trees, açaí and buriti palms, and slow brown channels and lagoons with floating meadows and giant water lilies, running on from tile to tile.",
  "about": "Biome for Amazon floodplain cells, made from the Mamirauá place research (game decision 0060, Muse inbox #239). Várzea is forest that the Solimões and Japurá flood each year, so the land is flat and wet: ponds cover at least a tenth of a tile and run on into the next, with flooded-forest shores. Its trees are written out (shape and colour) until stage C makes the species; then they go in plants by id. No named lakes, bogs or streams, so tiles do not repeat. Tropics: no seasons yet (the flood season can come later).",
